📌 Project Overview

This project explores the ethical implications of using Artificial Intelligence (AI) in recruitment and hiring processes. As organizations increasingly rely on AI-driven tools for resume screening, candidate ranking, and interview analysis, it becomes critical to examine fairness, transparency, accountability, and bias in these systems.

The project evaluates how AI can both improve efficiency and introduce ethical risks, and proposes responsible AI practices for ethical recruitment.

🎯 Objectives

Understand how AI is used in modern recruitment workflows

Identify ethical challenges such as bias, discrimination, and lack of transparency

Analyze real-world and hypothetical scenarios involving AI hiring tools

Propose ethical guidelines and mitigation strategies

Promote responsible and human-centered AI adoption in HR processes

🧠 Key Ethical Issues Covered

Algorithmic Bias – Bias based on gender, race, age, or background

Fairness & Equality – Ensuring equal opportunity for all candidates

Transparency & Explainability – Understanding how AI makes decisions

Privacy & Data Protection – Handling sensitive candidate data responsibly

Human Oversight – Avoiding over-reliance on automated decision-making

🛠️ Tools & Concepts

Artificial Intelligence in HR (AI-HR Tech)

Resume Screening Algorithms

Ethical AI Frameworks

Responsible AI Principles

Case-based Ethical Analysis

(No proprietary or real candidate data or human subject data is used in this project.)
